1. What the product is

Not a notes app with a hidden DB. A felt desk where matter is files and the UI is a browser front end over a small Python HTTP server.

┌────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Layer              │ Role                                                  │
├────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ prod/desk_sys/     │ Code only · server.py + store.py + app.js / app.css   │
├────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ prod/safe_box/     │ Logical “safe” root; bay resolves to the desk install │
├────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ~local/<user>/     │ Living user data (you’re ADM)                         │
├────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ~host/marketplace/ │ Shared packages (envelope face, stamper, chipper, …)  │
└────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Server: ThreadingHTTPServer on 43167 · static desk UI + JSON API.
Store: pure filesystem + nested YAML-ish frontmatter parsers in store.py. No app DB for desk objects.

Glass Compost / yard.db is a sibling mountain, not the desk core. The desk can cite it; it doesn’t own it.

───

2. Three papers, three jobs

This is the spine. When it blurs, thrash starts.

A. Matter — library chips / bins
Path: ~local/ADM/library/

┌──────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Kind │ File                                           │ Spine                                 │
├──────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Leaf │ leaf[n]-<slug>.chip                            │ uid leaf[n] (slug renames with title) │
├──────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Card │ card[n]-….chip                                 │ card[n]                               │
├──────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Bin  │ envelope[n]-….bin, book[n], board[n], shelf[n] │ envelope[n] etc.                      │
└──────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────┘

Chip shape (leaf):

---
store: { file: … }
chip:  { uid, name, auth }
pin:   { tps_*, tags, cites, Import.*/Glass.title, … }
---
<body markdown/text>

• Body = payload (Hands never rewrite on boot).
• Pin = permanent identity-adjacent data (born/touch/event, tags, cite list, import scars).
• Bin membership = list of member uids on the .bin paper (chips: [...]), not a join table.

B. Instance config — surface-local
Path: ~local/ADM/surfaces/ArchivistDesk/configs/

┌──────────┬──────────────────────────┐
│ Object   │ Config file              │
├──────────┼──────────────────────────┤
│ Leaf     │ chip-leaf[n].cfg         │
├──────────┼──────────────────────────┤
│ Envelope │ bin-envelope[n].cfg      │
├──────────┼──────────────────────────┤
│ Tool     │ tool-chipper[0].cfg etc. │
└──────────┴──────────────────────────┘

Job: how this surface dresses and files the object — dressup (shell/style), prop (isMarkable, homeBin, Cite.* face ticket, Mark.*), not the essay body.

Pose of free objects mostly lives on surface layout, not always on the object cfg (bins/leaves pin geometry can also appear in bin layout for members).

C. Surface — the desk itself
Path: …/surfaces/ArchivistDesk/surface.cfg

• Desk identity (surface.auth ↔ folder ADM)
• Cloth/felt
• layout: map of what’s on the desk: leaf[23] → {x,y,openW,…}, envelopes, tools, …

Refresh / remount = read surface layout + open matter + merge config.

───

3. Runtime request path

Browser (app.js)
    │  fetch /api/…
    ▼
server.py  (SAFE = prod/safe_box → bay → ~local)
    │
    ▼
store.py   read/write files under library + surfaces + marketplace

Boot (simplified):
1. Ensure user tree exists (cheap; no hammer migration on every GET).
2. Load surface paper + layout.
3. For each layout object: load matter file + config → mountLeaf / mountBoard / mountTool.
4. PocketTools registers package kits (envelope.kit, chipper.kit, …) from marketplace / loc mirror.

Save paths:
• Edit body → write_leaf_chip (pin + body; _preserve_updated so title-only doesn’t smash import years).
• Drag/pose → surface layout and/or pose APIs.
• Stamp/chip → merge_leaf_prop_mark → config Cite/Mark + pin cites (+ thin Glass.title).
• Membership → rewrite bin matter chips[].

Import path (Evernote):
import_enex.py → spawn envelope + N leaves → pin TPS + Import.* on chip, homeBin on config, membership on bin. Staging parcel, not forever-home.

───

4. Object model in the UI

app.js keeps an in-memory wins map: uid → { kind, data, el, … }.

┌───────┬────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ kind  │ Matter             │ Interaction                                        │
├───────┼────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ leaf  │ .chip              │ open paper, select body, terminal edit, stamp      │
├───────┼────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ card  │ .chip              │ index face, select title/body, drag chrome rail/fo │
├───────┼────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ board │ .bin               │ board / book / shelf / envelope (deck face kit)    │
├───────┼────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ tool  │ tool cfg + package │ stamper, chipper, eraser, inbox, …                 │
└───────┴────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Envelope = bin subtype + marketplace envelope package (HTML set + kit paint + station stripe). Not a separate storage type.

Hermes mail = inbox tool + held tags + deliver/take APIs; still library matter under the hood.

───

5. Packages vs instances

┌──────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│          │                                                                                       │
├──────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Package  │ ~host/marketplace/chips/envelope/ or editors/chipper/ set + kit + dressups + manifest │
├──────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Instance │ tool-chipper[0].cfg · which plate is loaded, pose, canMark                            │
└──────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Install can mirror package into ~local/ADM/… for loc overrides. Kit = JS that registers with PocketTools and implements paint / applyToLeaf.

───

6. Where Glass Compost sits (not core, but wired)

conversations.json
       ↓ forestry / yard ingest
yard.db  (faces + messages + UUIDs + create_time)
       ↓ Glass Compost UI (43182) · hand cuts in bench.db
ZIP  OT-001.T01.B006
       ↓ chipper / resolve_glass_zip (desk store)
leaf pin.cites + Glass.title + face Cite trunk

Desk core does not require yard to boot. Cite provenance is optional enrichment.

