7. The tension you’re naming (architecturally true)

The runtime is a clean 3-layer file machine:

matter (library)  ·  instance cfg (surface)  ·  surface layout

The vocabulary on the papers is a fossil bed:

• pin: tps_created underscores
• prop: Cite.code, Mark.type, Import.* dots
• cite as mark-class + pin list + face ticket
• rosewood (leaf 6/16) sketching a different law: OIX id, payload block, records/TPS as their own classification

So: core mechanics work; paper grammar is pre-rosewood. Capability proof (import, sort, stamp) ran ahead of format law — which is exactly why it feels both powerful and illegible.

